ration-card-update	Priority Ration Card Services (Ahara / Food & Civil Supplies)	Food, Civil Supplies and Consumer Affairs Department	food	Addition of newborn child/spouse, member address updates, fair price shop transfer, and cardholder detail corrections on BPL/APL ration cards.	Applicant must already hold a valid Karnataka Ration Card number in Ahara database.\nFor adding child: Birth certificate with parents’ names matching ration card.\nFor adding spouse: Marriage certificate and NOC/deletion certificate from previous ration card.\nAll members must have individual biometric Aadhaar numbers.	{"karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 14:27:14.68858+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.334365+00
gruha-lakshmi	Gruha Lakshmi Scheme (₹2,000 Monthly DBT)	Department of Women and Child Development	citizen	Direct monthly financial entitlement of ₹2,000 credited to the bank account of the designated woman head of household in BPL/APL families.	Applicant must be designated as the woman head of family on the ration card.\nOnly one woman per household is eligible.\nNeither the woman head of household nor her husband should be an income tax payer.\nNeither the woman nor her husband should be filing GST returns.	{"requiresFemaleHead": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 14:27:14.6997+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.342342+00
yuva-nidhi	Yuva Nidhi Scheme (Graduate & Diploma Stipend)	Department of Skill Development, Entrepreneurship and Livelihood	student	Monthly allowance of ₹3,000 for degree holders and ₹1,500 for diploma holders for up to two years during job-seeking and skill-upgradation.	Must have passed degree or diploma from a recognized university or board in Karnataka.\nMust have completed a minimum of 6 years of study in Karnataka (domicile requirement).\nMust have remained unemployed for at least 180 days after graduation results.\nMust not be pursuing higher education or employed in government/private sectors.\nMust not be self-employed or eligible for EPF/ESI benefits.	{"requiresStudent": false, "allowedOccupations": ["student"], "requiresUnemployed": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 14:27:14.704882+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.352191+00
ssp-scholarship	State Scholarship Portal (SSP) Post-Matric Scholarships	Social Welfare & Backward Classes Welfare Departments	student	Fee reimbursement, maintenance allowances, and examination fees for SC, ST, OBC, and minority students enrolled in post-matric colleges.	Applicant must be a bonafide student in a recognized Karnataka college / institute.\nMust possess a valid Student SATS ID / e-Attestation Number.\nAnnual family income ceiling: Up to ₹2.5 Lakh for SC/ST; Up to ₹1.0 Lakh for OBC (Cat-1, 2A, 2B, 3A, 3B).\nMust have verified Caste and Income Certificate RD numbers from Nadakacheri.	{"maxIncome": 250000, "requiresStudent": true, "allowedOccupations": ["student"], "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 14:27:14.710048+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.357213+00
arogya-karnataka	Arogya Karnataka (Ayushman Bharat — SAST)	Health and Family Welfare / Suvarna Arogya Suraksha Trust	health	Cashless secondary and tertiary hospitalization cover up to ₹5 lakh per year per family for BPL families and subsidized co-payment for APL families.	Permanent resident of Karnataka.\nMust possess an active BPL / PHH Ration Card for 100% free treatment or APL Card for co-payment.\nReferral from Government Primary Health Centre (PHC) / Taluk Hospital required for non-emergency tertiary care.	{"karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 14:27:14.715302+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.366829+00
msme-artisan-subsidy	Dr. B.R. Ambedkar Rural Micro-Enterprise & Artisan Subsidy	Commerce and Industries / Development Corporations	business	Financial margin-money subsidy up to ₹2.0 lakh for rural artisans, traditional craftsmen, and small micro-enterprises setting up local production.	Applicant must be aged 18 to 55 years and a permanent resident of Karnataka.\nMust have skill or vocational experience in proposed trade or artisan activity.\nAnnual household income must be below ₹2.0 lakh in rural areas.\nMust not have defaulted on any commercial or cooperative bank loan.	{"maxAge": 55, "minAge": 18, "maxIncome": 200000, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 14:27:14.72033+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.371359+00
kaveri-ec-services	Kaveri 2.0 — Property Encumbrance Certificate (EC) & Deeds	Department of Stamps and Registration	it_services	Instant digital application for Encumbrance Certificate (EC Form 15/16) and certified copies of registered land/property sale deeds.	Any citizen possessing property survey number, village/ward details, or registration deed number.\nNo income restriction applies.	{"karnatakaResidentOnly": false}	t	2026-11-10 14:27:14.72634+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.378821+00
pm-kisan	PM-KISAN (Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi)	Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare / Dept of Agriculture, Karnataka	farmer	Income support scheme providing ₹6,000 per year in three equal installments directly into the Aadhaar-seeded bank accounts of landholding farmer families across India.	All landholder farmer families who have cultivable landholding in their names.\nLand records must be verified in State FRUITS / Bhoomi database.\nExclusions: Institutional landholders, former/present constitutional post holders, income tax payers, and professionals (doctors, engineers, lawyers).	{"requiresLand": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": false}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.384216+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.384216+00
pm-fasal-bima	Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY)	Department of Agriculture, Govt. of Karnataka	farmer	Comprehensive yield and weather-based crop insurance scheme providing financial support to farmers suffering crop loss or damage arising from natural calamities, pests, and unseasonal rainfall.	All farmers cultivating notified crops in notified areas (both loanee and non-loanee farmers).\nTenant farmers and sharecroppers cultivating notified crops are eligible with tenancy documents.	{"requiresLand": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.388654+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.388654+00
krishi-bhagya	Krishi Bhagya Scheme (Farm Ponds & Polyhouse Subsidy)	Department of Agriculture, Govt. of Karnataka	farmer	Dryland agricultural support providing 80% to 90% subsidy for construction of farm ponds (Krishi Honda), polythene tarpaulin lining, diesel/solar pump sets, and micro-irrigation systems.	Farmer possessing minimum 1 acre dryland agricultural land in rainfed taluks of Karnataka.\nMust have registered landholding in Bhoomi portal with FRUITS ID.\nPriority given to small, marginal, and drought-affected farmers.	{"requiresLand": true, "requiresRural": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.398046+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.398046+00
ksheera-siri	Ksheera Siri Milk Producer Incentive Scheme	Department of Animal Husbandry & Fisheries / KMF	farmer	Government incentive of ₹5.00 per liter of milk supplied by dairy farmers to Karnataka Milk Federation (KMF) and District Milk Producers Cooperative Societies.	Must be a member of an affiliated Village Dairy Cooperative Society (MPCS).\nMust supply milk daily and maintain membership passbook.	{"requiresRural": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.40302+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.40302+00
gruha-jyothi	Gruha Jyothi Scheme (Free Domestic Electricity)	Energy Department, Govt. of Karnataka / ESCOMs	citizen	Flagship Karnataka welfare scheme providing up to 200 units of free domestic electricity per month to all residential households based on annual average consumption + 10%.	All residential households in Karnataka with a dedicated domestic electric meter connection.\nApplies to tenants and owners alike; only one meter connection per household is eligible.\nHousehold average consumption calculated from previous 12 months + 10% buffer.	{"karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.41185+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.41185+00
shakti-scheme	Shakti Scheme (Free Bus Travel for Women)	Transport Department, Govt. of Karnataka / KSRTC, BMTC, NWKRTC, KKRTC	citizen	100% free bus travel for all women, students, and transgender persons domiciled in Karnataka across state road transport corporation ordinary, express, and city bus services.	All women and transgender individuals domiciled in the State of Karnataka.\nNo income, age, or caste restrictions apply.	{"requiresFemaleHead": false, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.417898+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.417898+00
anna-bhagya	Anna Bhagya Scheme (Free Food Grains & Cash DBT)	Food, Civil Supplies and Consumer Affairs Department	food	Guarantees 10 kg of food grains per person per month for BPL and Antyodaya cardholders, comprising 5 kg free Central rice under NFSA + ₹170 per person per month DBT in lieu of State 5 kg rice.	Must hold an active BPL (Priority Household) or AAY (Antyodaya) ration card in Karnataka.\nHead of family must have Aadhaar-linked active bank account enabled for NPCI direct credit.	{"requiresBpl": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.422157+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.422157+00
ganga-kalyana	Ganga Kalyana Scheme (Free Irrigation Borewells)	Social Welfare / Backward Classes / Minorities Development Corporations	farmer	Provides free individual or community irrigation borewells, casing pipes, submersible pumps, and electricity energization for small/marginal farmers belonging to SC, ST, OBC, and Minority communities.	Applicant must belong to SC, ST, Backward Classes, or Minority community.\nMust possess minimum 1.5 to 5 acres of dry agricultural land (2 to 5 contiguous acres for group).\nAnnual family income must not exceed ₹1.5 lakh for rural areas (₹2.0 lakh for urban).\nNo other member of family should have availed Ganga Kalyana benefit earlier.	{"maxIncome": 150000, "requiresLand": true, "requiresRural": true, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.429856+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.429856+00
swavalambi-sarathi	Swavalambi Sarathi Vehicle Subsidy Scheme	Karnataka Minorities / Backward Classes Development Corporation	business	Provides 50% capital subsidy (up to ₹3.00 lakh) for unemployed youth purchasing commercial four-wheelers (taxis, passenger autos, delivery vans, tractors) through bank linkage.	Applicant aged 21 to 45 years belonging to Religious Minorities or Backward Classes.\nMust possess a valid Yellow Badge / Commercial Driving License (LMV-TR / Transport).\nAnnual family income must be below ₹3.50 lakh in rural areas.\nMust not have availed vehicle subsidy under any other state corporation.	{"maxAge": 45, "minAge": 21, "maxIncome": 350000, "karnatakaResidentOnly": true}	t	2026-11-10 17:59:45.433485+00	2026-11-10 17:59:45.433485+00
